<node id="1218145" title="Re^3: How to differentiate an empty array from an unitialized one?" created="2018-07-09 04:55:36" updated="2018-07-09 04:55:36" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;Split can return undef depending on regex capture groups &lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Yes, that's correct, for example &lt;c&gt;split( /(x)|(y)/, "axbyc" )&lt;/c&gt; yields &lt;c&gt;("a", "x", undef, "b", undef, "y", "c")&lt;/c&gt;. It's also documented at the bottom of [doc://split].&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
